WEBVTT

00:56.073 --> 00:58.868
FILING FOR LOVE

01:06.625 --> 01:08.919
SENDER: NONAME
TITLE: REPORTING MS. JOO IN-A

01:09.003 --> 01:10.921
SHE IS INVOLVED IN AN INAPPROPRIATE
WORKPLACE RELATIONSHIP

01:25.811 --> 01:27.563
HIDE SENDER ID
TITLE: REPORTING MS. JOO IN-A

01:27.646 --> 01:28.814
SHE IS INVOLVED IN
AN INAPPROPRIATE...

01:31.817 --> 01:32.943
SEND

01:33.527 --> 01:36.071
EMAIL WAS SENT SUCCESSFULLY

01:42.328 --> 01:43.787
MS. JOO IN-A

01:43.871 --> 01:45.122
...AN INAPPROPRIATE
WORKPLACE RELATIONSHIP

01:45.206 --> 01:47.875
HAEMU STRATEGIC PLANNING, MARKETING,
DIGITAL MARKETING, AUDIT TEAM 1, 2, 3

01:52.379 --> 01:55.508
SEND

02:02.431 --> 02:03.474
SECRETARY AHN SEUNG-HEE

02:06.352 --> 02:07.478
- Hey.
- A-jeong.

02:07.895 --> 02:09.647
Check out the article I just sent.

02:14.693 --> 02:17.488
HAEMU'S FIRSTBORN DRIVEN OUT?
SIBLING RIVALRY HEATS UP

02:18.739 --> 02:20.074
Did you call the PR Team?

02:20.157 --> 02:22.952
Look into the journalist
and find out how he got the story.

02:23.035 --> 02:24.286
I'll call Legal.

02:46.517 --> 02:47.518
In-a.

02:54.650 --> 02:57.111
Can I help you?
I'm cleaning the suite.

02:59.530 --> 03:00.614
You can't...

03:27.224 --> 03:28.892
You're gonna burn a hole
through my face.

03:30.436 --> 03:33.897
I know I'm a charming
and good-looking guy, but...

03:45.993 --> 03:47.077
What are you doing?

03:47.411 --> 03:48.579
Checking to see if you're real.

03:50.748 --> 03:53.751
How did you manage to show up
right at that moment?

03:56.962 --> 03:57.963
Unbelievable.

03:59.256 --> 04:00.424
What kind of moment was it?

04:00.758 --> 04:02.718
It was the moment I thought
that I wanted to see you.

04:07.306 --> 04:09.099
How could you say something
so heart-fluttering

04:10.684 --> 04:12.144
with such a straight face?

04:17.816 --> 04:18.942
I was regretting

04:19.818 --> 04:21.403
not being true to my feelings.

04:23.322 --> 04:25.074
I wanted to turn things back

04:25.699 --> 04:26.742
but thought it was too late.

04:27.368 --> 04:29.036
I was upset,
and it left me with regrets.

04:29.953 --> 04:31.163
But at the same time, I thought

04:31.997 --> 04:34.333
"Oh, I'd love to see
Ki-jun right now."

04:34.833 --> 04:37.294
Just when I was thinking that,
you appeared out of nowhere.

04:38.545 --> 04:40.089
I kind of knew that feeling

04:40.923 --> 04:43.133
so I rushed here
without wasting a second.

04:48.722 --> 04:50.808
Thank you for coming to get me.

04:56.897 --> 04:59.650
Let's turn things back one by one.

05:00.484 --> 05:01.610
I won't go to the US.

05:02.069 --> 05:03.404
I'm doing whatever it takes to stay.

05:03.904 --> 05:05.322
If you try to force me to go

05:05.823 --> 05:07.741
I'll lie down flat in the lobby
to protest so I can stay.

05:11.203 --> 05:15.708
The thing is, going to the US office
would be a great opportunity for you.

05:16.417 --> 05:18.043
Didn't we agree to be honest?

05:20.504 --> 05:21.839
Should I actually go?

05:24.341 --> 05:26.176
No, don't go.

05:26.468 --> 05:27.678
Stay right next to me.

05:29.388 --> 05:30.431
You bet.

05:50.701 --> 05:53.162
- That's it?
- Yes, that's it.

05:54.913 --> 05:55.998
What about the other side?

06:37.748 --> 06:40.417
What's this?
We only just said goodbye.

06:40.751 --> 06:41.752
Do you miss me already?

06:42.461 --> 06:44.505
Yes, I miss you.

06:47.758 --> 06:49.134
My heart almost burst.

06:49.426 --> 06:50.594
Over that?

06:51.470 --> 06:53.347
You should brace yourself.

06:53.972 --> 06:55.641
Once I start dating someone

06:55.724 --> 06:57.434
I get all passionate and fired up.

06:58.936 --> 07:00.437
I knew it.

07:00.979 --> 07:03.315
I should brace myself
to date someone like you.

07:05.108 --> 07:06.568
I'm not so easygoing either.

07:06.944 --> 07:09.530
So you should brace yourself as well.

07:09.696 --> 07:10.781
What, really?

07:11.615 --> 07:13.158
What should I prepare first?

07:15.911 --> 07:18.080
Why don't we figure out
what to call each other?

07:18.705 --> 07:20.833
I don't want
to have to call you "Ms. Joo."

07:20.916 --> 07:22.251
It's too formal and unfriendly.

07:24.419 --> 07:25.420
My darling In-a.

07:26.880 --> 07:27.881
In-a.

07:28.966 --> 07:30.551
Now that I think about it

07:30.968 --> 07:32.427
you have a beautiful name.

07:33.720 --> 07:34.763
Joo In-a.

07:37.307 --> 07:39.309
- Hi, guys.
- Hey.

07:43.021 --> 07:44.731
- Let's drink.
- Cheers.

07:49.862 --> 07:52.072
Jae-yeol, what's up with you?

07:52.155 --> 07:53.740
You never joined us
when we invited you before.

07:55.158 --> 07:56.493
I know I was too distant.

07:57.411 --> 07:58.620
Sorry about that.

07:59.705 --> 08:02.749
Hey, I think you should slow down.

08:02.833 --> 08:03.959
Aren't you drinking too much?

08:05.294 --> 08:09.047
Are you getting wasted because
your stepbrother was made co-VP?

08:09.214 --> 08:10.340
I read about that in the news.

08:10.674 --> 08:12.092
Your father's just...

08:12.676 --> 08:16.054
He could've just put things in order
instead of making him co-VP.

08:16.138 --> 08:17.931
It's like he put you two
in a cage to fight.

08:18.265 --> 08:20.642
You talk too much
when we're here to drink.

08:21.184 --> 08:22.811
- Drink up.
- Yes.

08:23.103 --> 08:25.188
Jae-yeol rarely joins us for drinks.

08:25.439 --> 08:27.691
- Let's drink.
- And get wasted.

09:21.411 --> 09:22.412
It's cold, isn't it?

09:23.413 --> 09:24.414
No.

09:29.753 --> 09:31.129
Do you like it that much?

09:32.047 --> 09:33.048
Yes.

09:35.884 --> 09:38.553
I can't believe I look forward
to going to work in the morning.

09:39.221 --> 09:40.222
For real?

09:40.722 --> 09:42.307
I love heading into work.

09:42.516 --> 09:44.685
Work is much more fun
than being bored at home.

09:45.185 --> 09:46.186
No wonder.

09:47.312 --> 09:48.939
You had a look of madness
in your eyes.

09:51.942 --> 09:55.862
We'll do more fun things together
other than just work.

09:56.697 --> 09:58.824
Clear your schedule this weekend.

09:59.741 --> 10:03.996
We went all the way to Jeju Island
but had to return right away.

10:04.746 --> 10:06.331
I booked a pool villa in Sokcho.

10:07.040 --> 10:09.668
Let's take our time
to play in the sea

10:10.127 --> 10:11.211
and get some fresh air.

10:12.796 --> 10:14.673
Is this an overnight trip?

10:19.469 --> 10:21.471
It's... Well...

10:21.763 --> 10:23.932
A one-day trip
won't leave us much time.

10:29.771 --> 10:30.856
I love it.

10:35.944 --> 10:37.654
I'm kind of worried

10:38.488 --> 10:40.907
that I won't be able to hide
how much I like you at work.

10:41.283 --> 10:43.368
- What should I do?
- I'd love to see that.

10:44.161 --> 10:45.162
Not being able to hide it.

10:47.789 --> 10:49.082
Don't smile like that.

10:49.291 --> 10:51.460
If you smile, I can't help but smile,
and my feelings will show.

10:54.838 --> 10:57.841
This is a serious matter.
It's going to be too obvious.

10:58.967 --> 11:00.552
Too obvious, my foot.

11:12.647 --> 11:13.982
Even when she's in a relationship

11:15.609 --> 11:19.029
Joo In-a was
still her old self at work.

11:20.030 --> 11:22.282
So what is your conclusion?

11:22.949 --> 11:25.243
It doesn't say on this page
or on this page.

11:26.453 --> 11:28.663
There's nothing.
This report has no key point!

11:29.623 --> 11:30.624
See this?

11:31.374 --> 11:33.460
Do you see a key point
in this report?

11:35.504 --> 11:39.049
This is the kind of report you should
pay to write, not be paid to write.

11:39.341 --> 11:40.383
It's a waste of paper.

11:41.510 --> 11:42.719
Rewrite the whole thing.

12:06.785 --> 12:08.161
Are you all right, Mr. Noh?

12:09.579 --> 12:10.580
Mr. Noh.

12:10.914 --> 12:12.749
Did you do something
to get on her nerves?

12:13.375 --> 12:15.919
No, it's because he's working
too much.

12:16.586 --> 12:18.672
Mr. Noh, be more like me.

12:19.673 --> 12:21.299
Talk more and do less.

12:21.383 --> 12:24.052
The more an auditor does,
the harder they get audited.

12:24.261 --> 12:26.263
The more you do,
the more there is to criticize.

12:28.014 --> 12:29.933
Those are such wise words.

12:30.475 --> 12:32.185
For someone who doesn't do much

12:32.269 --> 12:36.523
how do you end up with the most
overtime pay each month?

12:36.606 --> 12:38.358
Will you all stop it?

12:38.817 --> 12:39.818
Ms. Yoon.

12:40.235 --> 12:42.529
Did you finish the slides
for the presentation on our clubs?

12:42.612 --> 12:45.031
Yes, I emailed you the final version.

12:45.115 --> 12:46.324
Good job.

12:46.575 --> 12:50.245
Did you add as many photos, tables,
and animations as possible?

12:51.955 --> 12:53.707
I'm sure you did your job.

12:53.790 --> 12:54.791
Good for you.

12:55.125 --> 12:58.128
When we present the report
to Ms. Joo later

12:58.211 --> 12:59.588
you're all coming with me.

13:00.589 --> 13:01.631
You, too, Mr. Noh.

13:02.549 --> 13:05.218
Ms. Joo is a really nice person.

13:05.302 --> 13:06.595
Don't be too afraid of her.

13:07.429 --> 13:08.471
Okay.

13:09.806 --> 13:11.391
I'm sure she's a nice person.

13:17.898 --> 13:19.232
The problem is that she's too nice.

13:38.960 --> 13:39.961
Ms. Park?

13:41.630 --> 13:45.258
- Yes?
- When will VP Jeon be here?

13:46.092 --> 13:48.678
He isn't well today.

13:50.013 --> 13:52.515
I'll present the agenda instead.

13:56.728 --> 13:57.729
Okay.

13:58.480 --> 14:00.607
We can't wait forever.

14:08.490 --> 14:09.658
Let's start without him.

14:10.367 --> 14:13.245
Don't you forget
that I am a VP as well.

14:14.079 --> 14:16.706
Yes, I think
it would be fine to start.

14:17.415 --> 14:19.167
Ms. Park, you can leave.

14:19.251 --> 14:20.710
- But...
- Being a secretary

14:21.044 --> 14:24.047
doesn't give you the right
to attend in a VP's place.

14:41.314 --> 14:44.234
VICE PRESIDENT

14:47.445 --> 14:49.656
SECRETARY PARK A-JEONG

15:45.628 --> 15:48.381
- Gosh, the water...
- It's so clear.

15:49.466 --> 15:51.551
Were they rockfish? Did you see them?

15:51.634 --> 15:52.761
- Yes.
- There was a swarm.

15:52.844 --> 15:54.929
- It was amazing.
- Just fantastic.

15:55.513 --> 15:56.639
- Did you notice?
- Yes.

15:56.723 --> 15:58.016
- Right?
- Did you?

15:58.099 --> 15:59.392
- I saw.
- What was that?

16:00.226 --> 16:01.394
It was incredible.

16:01.895 --> 16:03.146
The water's so clear today.

16:03.438 --> 16:05.148
- It's a rare occasion.
- I know.

16:11.488 --> 16:12.864
- You're back.
- Yes.

16:13.281 --> 16:14.324
Did you have fun?

16:14.991 --> 16:16.242
Is Seo-yeon in bed?

16:16.534 --> 16:17.535
Yes.

16:18.703 --> 16:21.748
Her English kindergarten is hosting
a cooking class on the 29th.

16:21.831 --> 16:22.957
You can make it, right?

16:28.171 --> 16:30.173
- I have a club meeting on the 29th.
- Again?

16:30.632 --> 16:32.967
Why do you have to go
scuba diving that often?

16:35.887 --> 16:37.639
Can't you miss it for once?

16:38.181 --> 16:40.809
I went on my own
to Seo-yeon's speech contest.

16:40.892 --> 16:42.644
Do you know how upset she was
that you'd missed it?

16:42.727 --> 16:45.188
I'll be at the next one.

16:47.190 --> 16:48.983
Are you sure you go scuba diving?

16:49.692 --> 16:51.111
Are you up to something else?

17:08.420 --> 17:09.462
AUDIT SUMMARY

17:09.921 --> 17:14.426
We found four cases in which
clubs fraudulently enrolled

17:14.509 --> 17:18.054
new recruits or temporary staff
to collect extra club funds.

17:18.138 --> 17:21.641
And in seven cases,
club admin embezzled club funds

17:21.724 --> 17:24.477
rented spaces or paid instructors
for personal gain.

17:25.937 --> 17:28.231
We found eight malpractice cases
where club members

17:28.314 --> 17:30.900
hired businesses
run by friends or family.

17:30.984 --> 17:34.362
In two cases, there were issues
that constituted gambling.

17:36.406 --> 17:38.867
The in-house clubs currently hand in

17:38.950 --> 17:41.828
- an activity report yearly, right?
- Yes, that's right.

17:41.911 --> 17:45.665
Have them submit one each quarter
with more details in the report.

17:45.748 --> 17:47.041
Ask HR to make the announcement.

17:47.125 --> 17:48.751
Okay, I'll relay the message.

17:48.835 --> 17:51.921
We also have a club-related PM case.

17:53.798 --> 17:56.843
The wife of Min Tae-woo
at Haemu International contacted us.

17:56.926 --> 18:00.013
Her husband is way too active
in the scuba diving club.

18:00.096 --> 18:02.307
She's not entirely sure
their activities are wholesome.

18:02.390 --> 18:06.603
It's hard to tell because of the gear
but the man on the right is Mr. Min.

18:06.686 --> 18:09.814
The person on the right is
suspected to be his affair partner.

18:09.898 --> 18:12.567
The wife found many photos
of this person in particular.

18:12.650 --> 18:14.402
Aren't they just enjoying a hobby?

18:14.486 --> 18:16.196
It did seem somewhat odd.

18:16.279 --> 18:18.907
Mr. Min supposedly dislikes water
and didn't even swim.

18:18.990 --> 18:21.910
He goes scuba diving
almost every week now.

18:21.993 --> 18:24.370
He's known to even
take time off work to go.

18:24.454 --> 18:26.706
And at home,
he always says he's tired.

18:26.789 --> 18:29.501
Oh, and he gets calls at dawn
or in the middle of the night

18:29.584 --> 18:31.252
and jumps up to go out.

18:31.336 --> 18:34.339
Many complain
that company clubs foster affairs

18:34.422 --> 18:37.884
and that the company encourages it
by covering expenses.

18:37.967 --> 18:40.970
Why don't we make this an example
and look into this incident?

18:41.054 --> 18:43.932
We won't get anywhere
with what we have if they deny it.

18:46.184 --> 18:49.395
Let's attend a club outing
and see how things actually are.

18:51.064 --> 18:52.190
Mr. Noh.

18:52.607 --> 18:53.983
Do you know how to scuba-dive?

18:55.527 --> 18:57.904
I did take a few lessons
on a trip once.

18:57.987 --> 18:59.864
You should go to Mr. Min's club

18:59.948 --> 19:01.032
- this weekend.
- What?

19:04.661 --> 19:06.412
This weekend

19:07.830 --> 19:10.333
I have an important appointment.

19:12.377 --> 19:13.378
Do you?

19:14.337 --> 19:16.965
Is anyone else able to scuba-dive?

19:17.549 --> 19:19.676
Extended exposure to water
gives me a rash.

19:19.759 --> 19:21.010
- The sea...
- That's bad.

19:21.094 --> 19:23.429
I almost drowned in a river
as a child and the trauma...

19:23.513 --> 19:25.431
- I can't equalize underwater.
- I can't manage.

19:25.515 --> 19:27.225
I refuse to work on weekends.

19:27.308 --> 19:29.185
It verges on a rare disease.

19:29.894 --> 19:31.229
Oh, dear...

19:31.938 --> 19:33.439
I'm left with no choice, then.

19:34.190 --> 19:35.692
I love scuba diving.

19:36.901 --> 19:38.444
- I'll go.
- What?

19:38.528 --> 19:39.571
What?

19:45.868 --> 19:47.662
Don't you have anything planned

19:48.371 --> 19:50.290
for this weekend?

19:50.373 --> 19:52.750
I don't have
any special plans this weekend.

19:53.418 --> 19:55.044
Clear your schedule this weekend.

19:55.128 --> 19:56.796
I booked a pool villa in Sokcho.

19:56.879 --> 19:58.423
I thought I didn't have plans.

20:02.468 --> 20:03.886
You do have plans, then.

20:04.721 --> 20:06.347
How could you?

20:07.432 --> 20:10.643
Aren't you happy
we get to travel together?

20:11.269 --> 20:13.688
We're doing
exactly what we planned to do.

20:13.771 --> 20:15.106
We see the sea
and get some fresh air.

20:15.189 --> 20:16.733
- Plus, we get to work, too.
- Goodness.

20:16.816 --> 20:17.984
We hit two birds with one stone

20:18.067 --> 20:20.028
by going swimming
and seeing some fish.

20:20.111 --> 20:23.364
You said you get passionate
when you start dating.

20:23.448 --> 20:25.199
But all you did was
make me work passionately.

20:25.283 --> 20:27.785
I thought I was going
to burn to ashes with your passion.

20:27.869 --> 20:29.954
That was because we had a lot to do

20:30.038 --> 20:31.664
because of the previous week's trip.

20:31.748 --> 20:34.584
Also, I didn't want anyone at work
to notice anything.

20:34.792 --> 20:36.127
I put on an act with a poker face.

20:36.210 --> 20:38.880
You got so into that act
that you forgot our weekend plan.

20:40.882 --> 20:43.718
That was because it's been so long
since I made weekend plans.

20:44.385 --> 20:45.637
Plus, this is work.

20:45.720 --> 20:47.972
I'm very good at separating
work from my personal life.

20:48.056 --> 20:49.932
Yes, of course. I get it, Ms. Joo.

20:50.350 --> 20:52.769
We're on a business trip,
not a pleasure cruise.

20:52.852 --> 20:55.647
I'll make sure to act accordingly,
completely aloof and official.

20:58.900 --> 21:00.526
Ki-jun, are you actually angry?

21:01.402 --> 21:02.445
Yes.

21:04.072 --> 21:06.324
You fool. You twit.

21:06.574 --> 21:08.868
How could you forget your first date?

21:09.160 --> 21:10.912
- Get a grip, In-a!
- Don't.

21:10.995 --> 21:12.497
- What are you doing?
- What?

21:12.580 --> 21:13.790
I deserve a good scolding.

21:13.873 --> 21:17.335
- You fool. You twit. You moron.
- No, stop it. Don't do that.

21:17.418 --> 21:19.379
I was kidding, okay?

21:19.671 --> 21:21.506
I'm not angry at all. I was joking.

21:21.589 --> 21:23.883
- You seemed really angry.
- I wasn't.

21:23.966 --> 21:25.468
I wasn't even sulking.

21:26.052 --> 21:27.553
I'm really sorry.

21:28.012 --> 21:29.138
Don't be.

21:29.931 --> 21:31.474
Goodness...

21:37.063 --> 21:40.191
We have new members joining us today.

21:40.358 --> 21:43.319
It's Ms. Joo In-a, Head of Audit
from the head office

21:43.403 --> 21:45.822
and Assistant Manager Noh Ki-jun.

21:46.572 --> 21:48.991
- It's a pleasure to meet you all.
- Applause.

21:49.742 --> 21:51.828
You're both from the Audit Team

21:51.911 --> 21:53.705
so I feel somewhat nervous.

21:53.788 --> 21:57.959
We use our funds appropriately
and we do nothing wrong, do we?

21:58.042 --> 21:59.502
- Do you all agree?
- Yes.

21:59.585 --> 22:02.255
Club president, don't you know
saying that makes you look guilty?

22:03.005 --> 22:04.215
You have a point.

22:04.298 --> 22:07.844
We have a small group today,
so we'll go out together.

22:07.927 --> 22:09.846
Check your equipment thoroughly.

22:09.929 --> 22:11.097
- Okay.
- Okay.

22:11.305 --> 22:12.432
Get to it.

22:18.104 --> 22:19.313
Hey.

22:35.913 --> 22:36.998
Watch out.

22:37.081 --> 22:39.500
This valve here needs to be checked.

22:40.418 --> 22:42.086
We run on a buddy system.

22:42.170 --> 22:43.713
This is your first dive with us

22:43.796 --> 22:46.090
so you should partner
with someone more experienced.

22:46.340 --> 22:49.302
I will partner with Mr. Min, then.

22:49.469 --> 22:52.597
The way he's helping her
looks reliable and reassuring.

22:52.680 --> 22:55.558
Then Mr. Min, you'll go out with him.

22:55.641 --> 22:57.393
- Okay.
- Ms. Joo, your partner...

22:57.477 --> 22:58.644
I volunteer.

23:22.126 --> 23:24.128
Mr. Min and Ms. Ha seem pretty close.

23:24.754 --> 23:26.255
Yes, they do.

23:28.466 --> 23:30.843
Are you upset Ms. Ha
is his possible fling?

23:31.302 --> 23:32.345
What?

23:33.012 --> 23:36.474
You couldn't seem to take
your eyes off her.

23:36.557 --> 23:39.519
What does that mean work-wise?

23:40.520 --> 23:43.523
My eyes were not locked onto her.

23:44.649 --> 23:46.192
It's all work-related.

23:46.567 --> 23:50.738
I just wanted to confirm if she was
the other person in the photos.

23:51.864 --> 23:52.865
I'll see you later.

23:55.201 --> 23:56.327
Personal-wise.

24:00.414 --> 24:01.541
Gosh...

24:02.041 --> 24:04.544
Get ready to dive.
Get your equipment.

24:04.627 --> 24:05.711
- Okay.
- Okay.

24:06.462 --> 24:07.630
Be sure to check that.

24:08.714 --> 24:10.216
- Okay, checked.
- Good.

24:10.716 --> 24:12.468
- It's all done.
- Great.

26:33.526 --> 26:35.152
Are you all right?

26:47.289 --> 26:49.208
That seemed like a panic attack.

26:50.334 --> 26:52.420
Are you claustrophobic or something?

26:53.045 --> 26:55.423
I'm fine. It wasn't anything serious.

26:55.506 --> 26:57.091
Did you tell the instructor?

26:57.550 --> 27:00.803
You should inform the others
for their safety, too.

27:00.886 --> 27:02.346
It's not that serious, okay?

27:04.390 --> 27:09.729
Are you afraid you won't get to dive
if the others find out about this?

27:10.229 --> 27:11.647
Do you love to dive that much?

27:11.731 --> 27:14.108
You say too much
for someone who just joined.

27:14.734 --> 27:16.235
I can handle my business.

27:17.570 --> 27:18.863
Stay out of it.

27:36.589 --> 27:37.757
Oh, come on.

27:38.007 --> 27:39.425
It was a great dive.

27:40.551 --> 27:44.764
He braves panic attacks to dive
just so he can see a woman regularly?

27:45.806 --> 27:48.142
He could if he likes her that much.

27:48.225 --> 27:50.728
It makes for a good excuse
for them to spend time together.

27:52.521 --> 27:54.648
Ms. Ha is a veteran diver.

27:55.524 --> 27:57.526
This story makes more sense.

27:57.610 --> 27:59.236
Mr. Min fell for Ms. Ha first

27:59.320 --> 28:01.697
found out what her hobby was,
and joined the club.

28:03.866 --> 28:06.118
Gosh, if that's true

28:07.369 --> 28:09.038
he's risking his life
for just an affair.

28:10.122 --> 28:12.792
I'm so sorry about this.
I'd love to join you for dinner

28:12.875 --> 28:15.461
but I have to get back to attend
an old coworker's father's funeral.

28:15.544 --> 28:17.755
I had a great time today.
See you on the next dive.

28:17.838 --> 28:19.090
- Goodbye.
- Get back safely.

28:19.173 --> 28:20.925
- Bye.
- Sleep well.

28:21.008 --> 28:22.093
- Bye.
- Goodbye.

28:22.593 --> 28:23.969
What do we eat for dinner?

28:24.053 --> 28:26.097
We had so much fun
swimming with the fish.

28:26.180 --> 28:28.140
We're not eating raw fish, are we?

28:29.141 --> 28:30.476
How about a toast?

28:30.893 --> 28:32.895
- Good dive!
- Good dive!

28:32.978 --> 28:34.730
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

28:41.487 --> 28:43.114
They were friends only moments ago.

28:44.657 --> 28:45.866
Goodbye, little fishies.

28:48.494 --> 28:51.247
Ms. Joo is hilarious.
Don't you think?

28:54.375 --> 28:57.837
These aren't the fish we saw,
so there's no need to feel bad.

28:58.212 --> 28:59.880
The ssamjang here is the best.

29:00.548 --> 29:02.049
Here we go. Open up.

29:07.471 --> 29:08.639
Is it good?

29:13.686 --> 29:15.229
Mr. Noh, you, too. Open up.

29:16.981 --> 29:19.024
- What?
- Don't be shy.

29:19.358 --> 29:20.693
Open your mouth wide.

29:30.661 --> 29:32.246
That tastes amazing.

29:32.872 --> 29:35.124
Ms. Ha, your wraps are the best.

29:35.207 --> 29:37.751
Who taught you the recipe?

29:38.627 --> 29:39.712
It's so good.

30:05.613 --> 30:07.823
He drank enough alcohol
to kill himself.

30:08.449 --> 30:09.658
If you were any later

30:10.701 --> 30:11.994
something terrible could've happened.

30:39.772 --> 30:40.981
That's not going to happen.

30:42.608 --> 30:44.276
We can't go back
to how things used to be.

30:47.279 --> 30:48.364
What I'm trying to say is

30:49.823 --> 30:51.951
I'm never going back to you,
Jae-yeol.

31:07.841 --> 31:09.885
OUR DEEPEST CONDOLENCES

31:09.969 --> 31:11.804
MAY HE REST IN PEACE

31:14.682 --> 31:16.934
Are you recruitment peers
with Mr. Lee, then?

31:17.017 --> 31:18.477
He's one of the few guys
from the same batch.

31:18.560 --> 31:20.813
Right. You realize
that when you're at work

31:20.896 --> 31:22.898
your recruitment peer is
the closest you have to a friend.

31:22.982 --> 31:24.692
All my peers retired early

31:24.775 --> 31:26.193
- and recently, one...
- Mr. Han.

31:26.277 --> 31:28.195
- Long time no see.
- Hi, take a seat.

31:28.279 --> 31:30.197
- Hello.
- Let me introduce him, Mr. Moo.

31:30.281 --> 31:33.158
This is Yoon Sang-ho from Haemu
International Global Business Team.

31:33.742 --> 31:35.494
This is Audit Team's Leader
Moo Kwang-il.

31:35.577 --> 31:36.912
- It's a pleasure.
- Same here.

31:36.996 --> 31:38.956
I met two others
from your team today.

31:39.039 --> 31:41.792
I just got back
from the Scuba Diving Club

31:41.875 --> 31:45.879
and your head Ms. Joo
and Mr. Noh were there.

31:45.963 --> 31:47.756
- Oh, I see.
- Yes.

31:47.840 --> 31:50.551
- Let me pour you one.
- No, I drove here.

31:50.634 --> 31:52.386
- I'll pour you one instead.
- What a pity.

31:52.469 --> 31:54.555
- Not at all.
- Didn't you drive here

31:54.638 --> 31:57.891
- if you just got back from a trip?
- I can always hire a driver.

31:57.975 --> 31:59.852
- It's an honor to meet you.
- Same here.

32:04.315 --> 32:05.899
What's up with Ms. Ha?

32:06.608 --> 32:08.569
She stuck close to Mr. Min

32:09.028 --> 32:11.238
but then
she seemed interested in you, too.

32:11.572 --> 32:16.368
Well, I'm usually at the center
of everyone's attention.

32:16.452 --> 32:19.246
Is she the type who wants to get
all the men's attention?

32:20.914 --> 32:23.751
It's not all men, but me.

32:24.585 --> 32:26.086
It's because I'm Noh Ki-jun.

32:27.880 --> 32:29.256
It's Min and Ha.

32:36.221 --> 32:40.768
He's loading her equipment
into his car, isn't he?

32:42.061 --> 32:43.687
Something's up with them.

32:54.114 --> 32:55.115
Wait.

32:55.991 --> 32:57.451
Is he driving off with the equipment?

32:58.660 --> 32:59.661
Yes.

32:59.745 --> 33:02.456
It looks like Mr. Min
got a call from someone.

33:05.125 --> 33:06.210
Where's Ms. Ha?

33:23.685 --> 33:25.396
I'm really sorry.

33:25.479 --> 33:27.981
I get carsick easily
and can't sit in the back.

33:28.816 --> 33:31.026
Plus, that's usually
where the boss sits, right?

33:31.652 --> 33:32.861
You're the boss.

33:33.654 --> 33:35.322
I appreciate that.

33:35.406 --> 33:36.740
By the way...

33:37.491 --> 33:39.493
Where do you live, Mr. Noh?

33:39.743 --> 33:41.870
- What?
- Do you live nearby?

33:42.913 --> 33:46.250
I hope you don't have to make
too long a detour.

33:46.333 --> 33:48.168
I don't. It's fine.

33:49.878 --> 33:50.921
I have a question.

33:53.507 --> 33:57.094
Don't you dislike joining a club
with your direct superior?

33:57.177 --> 33:58.679
Oh, gosh. I can hear every word.

33:59.555 --> 34:01.014
My bad.

34:02.182 --> 34:04.393
Our dear Mr. Min's having a hard time

34:04.476 --> 34:08.021
because his superior Mr. Yoon
is in the same club.

34:14.278 --> 34:17.865
You and Mr. Min must be really close.

34:18.574 --> 34:20.701
You talked so much earlier today

34:20.784 --> 34:23.704
and just now you called him
"our dear Mr. Min."

34:24.496 --> 34:25.539
Oh, gosh.

34:27.291 --> 34:28.625
You got the wrong idea.

34:30.043 --> 34:32.880
Mr. Min's married with a kid.

34:33.213 --> 34:34.756
We're second cousins.

34:35.466 --> 34:37.384
It's a pure coincidence
that we joined the same club.

34:38.218 --> 34:40.512
Then you and Mr. Min

34:41.054 --> 34:42.639
are just relatives?

34:42.973 --> 34:46.518
Yes, that's why I loaded
my equipment in his trunk.

34:47.561 --> 34:49.897
Wait, what? Are you serious?

34:50.230 --> 34:51.899
Where did you get that idea?

34:52.858 --> 34:56.361
Hey, you must
be working out, Mr. Noh.

34:56.445 --> 34:58.655
Gosh, that's just hilarious.

34:58.739 --> 35:00.782
I almost got the wrong idea
about you two.

35:00.866 --> 35:03.702
It's so funny how things may seem.

35:03.785 --> 35:05.078
Goodness...

35:10.751 --> 35:13.378
So in the end, that new recruit

35:13.462 --> 35:16.548
raided HR and made a huge fuss,
which resulted in

35:16.632 --> 35:19.843
kicking out Mr. Lee
to another branch.

35:19.927 --> 35:23.013
These days,
people call everything gaslighting.

35:23.096 --> 35:24.515
We can't even talk anymore.

35:24.598 --> 35:26.558
These kids only learned
the worst in everything.

35:26.642 --> 35:28.727
I'm sure there was a situation...

35:28.810 --> 35:30.729
It doesn't matter
what the situation is.

35:30.812 --> 35:33.899
How dare some rookie dare
to kick the department head out?

35:33.982 --> 35:35.317
How can this happen?

35:35.567 --> 35:38.529
Mr. Moo, if this happened in the army

35:38.612 --> 35:42.324
it'd be like a private messing
with the division commander. Jeez.

35:42.407 --> 35:44.868
Well, the office
isn't the same as the army.

35:45.118 --> 35:46.954
I mean, are they any different?

35:47.037 --> 35:48.872
They're both organizations,
and there are ranks.

35:48.956 --> 35:52.292
If so, we must also establish
proper discipline.

35:52.376 --> 35:54.670
That's what I'm trying to say.

35:54.753 --> 35:58.882
I thought you'd be more open-minded
because you're called the Global Team

35:58.966 --> 36:01.301
but you're even more old-fashioned
than a Korean Audit Team.

36:01.718 --> 36:03.178
Well, old-fashioned?

36:03.262 --> 36:05.889
When we have team dinners,
we don't even drink regular soju.

36:05.973 --> 36:08.642
We only get the red caps,
the ones with more alcohol content.

36:09.726 --> 36:10.936
Goodness, look at the time.

36:11.019 --> 36:12.729
- Please excuse me. Okay?
- You're leaving?

36:12.813 --> 36:15.065
Yes, I'll leave
after saying goodbye to Mr. Lee.

36:15.148 --> 36:16.608
- Eat up, then.
- Thanks.

36:16.692 --> 36:18.652
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

36:21.280 --> 36:23.282
- Hello.
- At our club today...

36:23.365 --> 36:25.075
I told you to learn
how to scuba dive, didn't I?

36:25.158 --> 36:27.828
I became acquainted
with the famous Head of Audit

36:27.911 --> 36:29.246
Joo In-a, and met everyone.

36:29.329 --> 36:31.331
I'll introduce her to you soon.

36:31.999 --> 36:34.042
Mr. Moo isn't too resourceful.

36:34.126 --> 36:35.919
There's no way
he's becoming an executive.

36:36.712 --> 36:38.589
But he's a good man.

36:38.672 --> 36:40.841
My friend, there's no use
in living as a good man.

36:43.176 --> 36:44.511
Anyway, one second.

36:45.345 --> 36:46.680
Hey, did you arrive?

36:47.097 --> 36:49.766
Yes, okay. Come to the car. Okay.

36:50.100 --> 36:53.020
- Sorry, my chauffeur's here.
- Okay. Bye.

36:55.105 --> 37:00.152
Jeez. It was awful to listen to him
badmouth people for hours.

37:03.071 --> 37:04.698
Wait. That's...

37:05.365 --> 37:06.992
That's Mr. Min
from the Scuba Diving Club.

37:08.076 --> 37:09.453
Is he waiting for someone?

37:18.378 --> 37:19.504
What?

37:20.005 --> 37:22.674
The chauffeur service Mr. Yoon called
was actually Mr. Min?

37:23.091 --> 37:24.217
Not a hire?

37:25.010 --> 37:26.470
Goodness, that guy.

37:27.596 --> 37:30.307
See? I knew it the moment
he badmouthed those people.

37:31.016 --> 37:32.851
What an awful man.

37:36.188 --> 37:37.481
Mr. Noh, it's me.

37:37.564 --> 37:39.399
I'm calling
about Mr. Yoon of the Global Team.

37:39.483 --> 37:40.859
He's an awful man.

37:52.537 --> 37:53.664
Mr. Yoon.

37:54.623 --> 37:56.375
- Mr. Yoon.
- Man.

37:57.042 --> 37:58.794
I had too much to drink.

37:59.211 --> 38:00.379
One moment.

38:06.677 --> 38:07.886
Gosh.

38:15.894 --> 38:17.187
- I got it.
- Yes, sir.

38:18.146 --> 38:19.981
- And the key. One second.
- Right.

38:21.692 --> 38:22.901
You should have this hangover cure.

38:22.984 --> 38:25.320
Man, that's my Native Speaker.

38:25.404 --> 38:26.446
You're right on.

38:33.662 --> 38:35.580
- Native Speaker.
- Yes, sir.

38:35.664 --> 38:37.624
I've got your back until the very end

38:37.708 --> 38:39.209
so just trust and follow me.

38:39.292 --> 38:42.003
You know I'm the only one who
looks after you in the office, right?

38:42.087 --> 38:43.463
Yes, of course.

38:43.839 --> 38:46.216
I'm always grateful for you.

38:46.800 --> 38:48.677
- Give me. And go.
- Yes, sir.

38:51.388 --> 38:52.472
Mr. Yoon.

38:53.890 --> 38:54.933
Well...

38:55.350 --> 38:57.519
About the diving schedule
next Saturday.

38:57.936 --> 38:58.937
What?

38:59.646 --> 39:01.606
- You can't come?
- Well, it's my kid.

39:02.399 --> 39:04.776
- The kindergarten has a class...
- Hey.

39:04.860 --> 39:06.611
Who am I going to team up with, then?

39:06.695 --> 39:09.948
I was really pissed partnering up
with that punk, the club president.

39:10.031 --> 39:11.783
He'd stop me
from going anywhere I want to

39:11.867 --> 39:14.286
and ring the bell
whenever I try to grab something.

39:14.369 --> 39:17.581
So? Is it too big a burden
to go diving with me every week?

39:17.664 --> 39:18.665
Am I forcing you?

39:18.749 --> 39:20.333
No, Mr. Yoon. That's not the case.

39:21.042 --> 39:22.919
Thanks to you,
I get to enjoy a wonderful hobby.

39:23.920 --> 39:25.088
Yes, kid.

39:25.881 --> 39:27.507
So just follow my footsteps, okay?

39:27.758 --> 39:30.302
You need to get promoted to manager
this time, don't you?

39:30.385 --> 39:32.345
You're the last one
among your recruitment peers.

39:33.305 --> 39:34.681
Yes, you're right.

39:35.515 --> 39:36.808
I'll try even harder.

39:36.892 --> 39:39.311
Don't just try hard, you punk.

39:40.103 --> 39:41.646
Do it well.

39:43.273 --> 39:45.066
Yes, sir. I'll do it well.

39:45.150 --> 39:46.777
Good, Native Speaker.

39:47.360 --> 39:49.070
- Go, now.
- Yes. Goodnight, sir.

39:49.154 --> 39:50.155
Yeah.

40:03.502 --> 40:04.711
Mr. Min.

40:14.012 --> 40:16.598
I heard Mr. Yoon calling you
"Native Speaker."

40:17.057 --> 40:18.391
What does he mean by that?

40:18.475 --> 40:21.686
Everyone in my team has been abroad
except for me.

40:22.187 --> 40:23.939
So they say
I'm the native Korean speaker

40:24.314 --> 40:25.690
and nicknamed me Native Speaker.

40:29.236 --> 40:31.488
It doesn't sound like
a pleasant nickname.

40:31.863 --> 40:34.241
Mr. Min, we saw it all.

40:34.574 --> 40:36.576
We saw you acting
as Mr. Yoon's designated driver.

40:37.285 --> 40:39.830
And you don't like scuba diving

40:40.038 --> 40:41.498
yet you continue doing it
to serve him.

40:41.581 --> 40:43.542
It's just office politics.

40:43.959 --> 40:45.502
Everyone does this.

40:45.585 --> 40:46.753
No, Mr. Min.

40:47.295 --> 40:49.381
That's considered
workplace harassment.

40:50.257 --> 40:51.341
She's right.

40:51.675 --> 40:54.344
You should use this chance
to speak up honestly.

40:55.220 --> 40:57.097
- Even to your wife.
- To my wife?

40:58.515 --> 41:00.433
No, that is something I cannot do.

41:00.517 --> 41:03.436
Your wife took this the wrong way
and thinks you're having an affair.

41:03.520 --> 41:05.272
I'd rather live
with the misunderstanding.

41:05.355 --> 41:06.356
Sorry?

41:07.482 --> 41:09.651
I don't want my wife to find out

41:11.903 --> 41:13.822
that this is
how I'm being treated at work.

41:14.865 --> 41:16.116
Right...

41:26.251 --> 41:27.294
I don't think

41:28.169 --> 41:30.338
this is a matter we can let slide.

41:30.422 --> 41:32.340
This isn't just a power dynamic.

41:32.424 --> 41:33.842
It's gaslighting.

41:33.925 --> 41:36.636
I can also understand why
he doesn't want his family to know.

41:36.720 --> 41:39.097
Let's just tell his wife
that we confirmed that

41:39.180 --> 41:40.223
he isn't having an affair.

41:40.974 --> 41:41.975
Okay.

41:42.058 --> 41:43.977
Also, it looks like Mr. Min

41:44.060 --> 41:46.396
needs to be separated
from Mr. Yoon as soon as possible.

41:47.105 --> 41:48.857
I'll try to think of a way.

41:51.359 --> 41:54.613
This isn't something
he can handle personally.

41:55.906 --> 41:58.325
There must be something
that the company can do.

42:11.171 --> 42:13.381
VNow, we're home.

42:14.174 --> 42:15.717
Time to stop thinking today.

42:15.800 --> 42:17.177
Go home and get some rest.

42:17.385 --> 42:19.137
You must be tired
after diving early in the morning.

42:20.847 --> 42:21.932
Mr. Noh.

42:24.017 --> 42:25.310
Do you want to stay for ramyeon?

42:48.208 --> 42:49.542
That's three minutes.

42:50.585 --> 42:53.046
Now, take a break
and have some ramyeon.

42:54.172 --> 42:55.298
Hey, wait.

42:55.382 --> 42:58.635
Since when did the phrase,
"Do you want to stay for ramyeon?"

42:59.094 --> 43:02.180
come to mean, "Why don't you
eat ramyeon and work all night?"

43:02.263 --> 43:04.683
The meaning has changed a while ago.
You didn't know?

43:06.393 --> 43:07.936
Now, eat up.

43:09.688 --> 43:12.565
And this isn't even actually boiled.
It's cup ramyeon.

43:13.108 --> 43:14.776
With no kimchi or pickled radish?

43:14.859 --> 43:17.737
Hey, you picked out good ones
in a short amount of time.

43:18.071 --> 43:20.115
But this definition
is a bit too abstract.

43:20.198 --> 43:22.534
You should specify
the actual relevant laws here.

43:22.826 --> 43:25.870
It'll be more effective
to present these examples verbally.

43:25.954 --> 43:27.414
Can you add images
and make it more visual?

43:31.626 --> 43:33.712
Give me some time to eat ramyeon.

43:33.795 --> 43:35.463
Isn't this example too much?

43:35.547 --> 43:37.382
Is there anything more universal?

43:40.802 --> 43:43.680
- What? Which one?
- This one.

43:44.305 --> 43:47.308
Workplace harassment
always starts quietly.

43:47.767 --> 43:51.688
It begins with a good morning
and an exchange of a glance.

43:52.564 --> 43:54.524
Then you slowly
become excluded from the team

43:54.607 --> 43:56.693
or get forced to do
an unreasonable amount of overtime.

43:57.152 --> 43:59.029
Sometimes the perpetrator goes,
"You can handle that."

43:59.112 --> 44:01.072
But other times, they go,
"Why do you do things your way?"

44:01.156 --> 44:02.407
"Do you think work is a joke?"

44:05.035 --> 44:06.536
What's truly scary is this.

44:06.619 --> 44:08.079
As these instances continue

44:08.163 --> 44:10.540
the victim begins
to blame themselves.

44:10.957 --> 44:12.459
"Am I the weird one?"

44:12.709 --> 44:14.002
"Am I too sensitive?"

44:14.085 --> 44:15.253
"Do people hate me?"

44:15.336 --> 44:16.671
THE VICTIM'S PSYCHOLOGICAL CHANGES

44:16.755 --> 44:19.799
This kind of anxiety makes the victim
accept such absurd requests.

44:23.928 --> 44:25.013
Everyone.

44:25.722 --> 44:28.058
The absurd one
is always the perpetrator.

44:28.475 --> 44:30.310
Do not doubt yourself or hesitate.

44:30.393 --> 44:32.312
Also, do not hide but report it.

44:33.980 --> 44:36.232
The company is obligated
to guard and protect

44:36.316 --> 44:38.276
the valued human resources
of its workplace.

44:40.070 --> 44:41.196
Do you understand?

44:41.279 --> 44:42.405
- Yes.
- Yes.

44:46.993 --> 44:48.495
Excuse me, Mr. Noh.

44:50.330 --> 44:52.290
- Hello, Mr. Min.
- Hello.

44:53.416 --> 44:56.211
Actually, I got the chance
to go to the US as an expatriate.

44:57.629 --> 44:58.630
Congratulations.

44:59.506 --> 45:02.133
I heard the opportunity
was originally meant for you.

45:02.217 --> 45:03.843
I hope you didn't have to step back
because of me.

45:03.927 --> 45:06.096
That's not something
I can just give up to someone.

45:06.513 --> 45:09.057
You're going because you are
more than qualified for the job.

45:10.183 --> 45:11.434
Thank you.

45:11.518 --> 45:14.646
Also, I saw that
Mr. Yoon got disciplined.

45:15.063 --> 45:16.940
- Is it because of me?
- Oh, no.

45:17.398 --> 45:19.109
We confirmed an instance of him

45:19.192 --> 45:21.861
leaving his workplace
during a business trip to go diving.

45:22.237 --> 45:24.906
That's why he got disciplined.
So don't worry about it.

45:24.989 --> 45:26.699
I see. Is that right?

45:28.034 --> 45:29.410
Have fun while you work abroad.

45:29.494 --> 45:31.538
I hope you go there
and get revitalized.

45:31.621 --> 45:32.664
I will.

45:33.206 --> 45:34.666
My wife is thrilled.

45:36.000 --> 45:37.210
I'll have a good time.

45:39.379 --> 45:40.421
Also

45:41.131 --> 45:42.257
you two look great together.

45:43.174 --> 45:44.968
- Sorry?
- Well...

45:56.563 --> 45:58.648
You can notice lots of things
when you're underwater.

46:00.150 --> 46:01.484
Even as you were diving with me

46:01.568 --> 46:03.153
your attention and mind

46:03.403 --> 46:05.196
were all on Ms. Joo over there.

46:06.197 --> 46:08.700
You kept my secret

46:09.200 --> 46:10.743
so I will keep yours, too.

46:11.327 --> 46:12.495
Don't worry.

46:12.829 --> 46:14.330
- Thank you.
- Sure.

46:18.918 --> 46:20.378
Nice shot!

46:22.005 --> 46:24.299
- You're ready to go out and play.
- Thank you, sir.

46:24.465 --> 46:27.510
I think I can play even better,
thanks to your lessons.

46:28.303 --> 46:29.637
Yes, right.

46:29.721 --> 46:31.723
I looked up the case
on Haemu Pharmaceutical

46:31.806 --> 46:33.433
and I did not get anything
during the handover.

46:33.725 --> 46:37.562
Really? Despite all those many audits

46:38.229 --> 46:39.647
there are no documents left behind?

46:40.064 --> 46:42.525
Yes. By any chance,
are you more concerned

46:42.734 --> 46:46.196
because Vice President Jeon Jae-yeol
was the previous president there?

46:48.239 --> 46:49.407
I don't know.

46:53.369 --> 46:55.330
Nice shot!
It's going straight to the pin!

46:55.747 --> 46:57.874
You got it right next to the hole.

46:58.374 --> 46:59.417
Gosh.

46:59.500 --> 47:01.252
Man, I already said
I came to play golf.

47:03.963 --> 47:05.089
Hey, what's up?

47:07.842 --> 47:08.968
Really?

47:09.636 --> 47:11.262
My sister-in-law is back?

47:41.042 --> 47:42.627
Is it because it's been a while?

47:43.211 --> 47:44.879
You look kind of pretty
when you sleep.

47:45.672 --> 47:47.006
I heard you got sick.

47:47.674 --> 47:49.342
Acute alcohol intoxication?

47:50.218 --> 47:52.470
Didn't you tell me
to get my addiction treated?

47:52.553 --> 47:54.931
This is freaking hilarious.

47:57.100 --> 47:58.142
When did you return?

47:58.226 --> 48:00.019
Dad gave me a hard time

48:00.103 --> 48:02.689
about being abroad
while you were in this mess.

48:03.982 --> 48:05.233
Anyway, what happened?

48:07.277 --> 48:09.779
I'm sure it wasn't because
you missed me so much.

48:11.656 --> 48:13.074
Were you that pissed

48:13.157 --> 48:14.951
about your brother becoming
co-vice president?

48:15.451 --> 48:16.953
Are you serious?

48:20.832 --> 48:23.126
What is this? You're boring.

48:23.543 --> 48:24.544
Hyun-young.

48:26.254 --> 48:27.297
Yes?

48:28.298 --> 48:29.424
Let's call it quits.

48:29.799 --> 48:30.800
What?

48:36.264 --> 48:37.348
Let's get divorced.

48:37.890 --> 48:39.392
What is this nonsense?

48:40.351 --> 48:41.936
Why should we get divorced?

48:42.020 --> 48:43.521
You're unhappy with me too.

48:45.690 --> 48:47.108
It's time to free each other.

48:49.485 --> 48:50.903
Let me know when you've decided.

48:52.405 --> 48:54.449
We can discuss the rest
through our lawyers.

48:59.287 --> 49:01.581
Hey, you have to tell me the reason.

49:01.956 --> 49:04.625
You and I didn't get married
to be happy, anyway.

49:05.376 --> 49:07.086
Why are you suddenly doing this?

49:07.337 --> 49:09.088
Have you finally lost it
just like your mom?

49:12.091 --> 49:13.968
I no longer want to live like this.

49:16.554 --> 49:17.638
You know you have

49:19.849 --> 49:22.393
zero chance at becoming the successor
if you divorce me, right?

49:25.146 --> 49:26.272
Hyun-young.

49:28.274 --> 49:29.901
I'll manage my own life.

49:30.985 --> 49:32.278
So please

49:33.446 --> 49:34.822
just divorce me.

49:51.506 --> 49:54.133
Hey, my husband is acting weird.

49:56.302 --> 49:57.595
Can you do some digging?

50:05.436 --> 50:08.064
When do you get off work?
Come to my place for dinner.

50:08.147 --> 50:09.190
JOO IN-A

50:09.273 --> 50:11.609
Why? Are you telling me
to stop by for ramyeon again?

50:18.533 --> 50:20.618
Today is the real deal.

50:26.916 --> 50:29.168
Great work today, everyone.

50:29.585 --> 50:30.878
- Great work today.
- Great work today.

50:34.090 --> 50:35.341
What was that?

50:35.425 --> 50:36.843
I think Ms. Joo just winked at me.

50:36.926 --> 50:39.053
- What?
- You must've seen something weird.

50:39.137 --> 50:41.931
Or she must've squinted
because she had something in her eye.

50:42.014 --> 50:43.933
No, I'm serious.

50:46.018 --> 50:47.937
- She did this.
- Do you think

50:48.438 --> 50:49.981
this is a sign of some sort?

50:50.064 --> 50:52.942
For what? Like, "You are sealed
for overtime tomorrow"?

50:53.025 --> 50:54.902
Her eyes must've stung.

50:54.986 --> 50:57.029
Stop talking nonsense. All right.

50:57.530 --> 50:59.490
We never got a chance to have

50:59.574 --> 51:01.492
a proper team dinner
after Mr. Noh got discharged.

51:01.951 --> 51:04.162
Why don't we go out
and eat something delicious?

51:04.245 --> 51:05.663
- Okay.
- I'd love to.

51:05.746 --> 51:07.415
Ms. Yoon?

51:07.498 --> 51:09.750
Well, it depends on what we eat.

51:09.834 --> 51:12.170
Oh, my.
I can't believe she's saying that.

51:13.588 --> 51:15.882
We need to eat
something really good today, then.

51:16.215 --> 51:18.718
It's been a while, so I'll let us use
the corporate card!

51:19.093 --> 51:21.095
- All right!
- Are we unleashing the company card?

51:21.179 --> 51:22.472
That means we have to go.

51:22.555 --> 51:23.723
- Let's go.
- Wait.

51:26.100 --> 51:27.602
I'm so sorry, but today...

51:29.479 --> 51:32.106
I really want to go, too.

51:35.026 --> 51:36.861
But I have an important appointment.

51:38.946 --> 51:40.281
I see.

51:41.866 --> 51:43.826
It's okay. We can work overtime.

51:43.910 --> 51:45.411
- Yes.
- Me too.

51:48.122 --> 51:50.333
- Overtime it is, then.
- It is.

51:57.298 --> 51:58.716
Let's see.

52:07.350 --> 52:10.394
Oh, my. What brings you
to the 14th floor, Ms. Park?

52:11.145 --> 52:13.064
I had to deliver something
to the Planning Team.

52:13.147 --> 52:14.524
Is that so?

52:29.580 --> 52:31.207
You must be enjoying yourself...

52:35.253 --> 52:36.546
caught between two men.

52:41.425 --> 52:42.760
Among the two men

52:43.094 --> 52:45.012
exactly which one
are you furious about?

52:45.263 --> 52:48.307
If I tell you,
will you let me have one of them?

52:49.433 --> 52:52.311
In that case,
it doesn't have to be Ki-jun.

52:52.979 --> 52:55.189
There's no need to do that.

52:56.566 --> 52:57.733
You two will be over shortly.

52:58.526 --> 53:00.778
That's how he handles
all his romantic relationships.

53:01.571 --> 53:02.572
Very casual.

53:07.118 --> 53:08.119
Let's say

53:09.453 --> 53:11.247
I back down from Jeon Jae-yeol.

53:12.123 --> 53:13.749
Can you even have him, A-jeong?

53:15.710 --> 53:17.587
I get that you're upset because of me

53:18.087 --> 53:19.380
but try not to cross the line.

53:19.839 --> 53:21.549
I may look quite young

53:21.632 --> 53:23.384
but I am an executive member
of this company.

53:23.926 --> 53:25.219
Executive Assistant Park A-jeong.

53:32.101 --> 53:33.102
Excuse me.

53:39.609 --> 53:42.778
- The White Blood Cell show!
- The White Blood Cell show!

53:48.326 --> 53:49.327
Go.

53:49.785 --> 53:51.245
Hey, how do you do that?

53:51.329 --> 53:52.997
Open up your throat

53:53.289 --> 53:54.540
and throw it in.

53:54.624 --> 53:56.709
Give me just a little bit of time.

53:57.043 --> 53:58.794
I'll be there soon
after I humor them.

53:58.878 --> 54:00.421
That's so amazing.

54:00.630 --> 54:04.425
- I mean, how do you do this?
- It's not a big deal.

54:05.051 --> 54:08.054
- You could even do an eating show.
- He could.

54:08.137 --> 54:10.473
Why won't the meat get cooked?
Is the heat too weak?

54:10.556 --> 54:12.058
No, it's the highest.

54:12.141 --> 54:14.602
It's taking a while
because the cut is so thick.

54:15.269 --> 54:17.021
Give me that. I'll do it.

54:17.104 --> 54:19.482
- No, I'll do it.
- It's okay. I'm on a diet, anyway.

54:19.565 --> 54:20.941
- I'll do it.
- No, I...

54:21.025 --> 54:22.360
- Give me that too.
- Goodness.

54:23.486 --> 54:25.988
All right! Eat your meat! Hurry!

54:26.072 --> 54:27.657
- All right!
- I'd love to!

54:27.740 --> 54:29.158
Eat up your meat!

54:29.241 --> 54:30.701
- I will.
- All right.

54:39.669 --> 54:40.753
Thanks.

54:43.130 --> 54:45.091
Do you not need
a toothbrush and a razor?

54:45.800 --> 54:48.094
- What?
- Aren't you having a hot night?

54:48.552 --> 54:49.762
You have to grab a toothbrush

54:49.970 --> 54:50.971
for your partner.

54:53.140 --> 54:54.975
It's been so long for me.

54:55.768 --> 54:57.019
Where can I find one?

54:57.436 --> 54:59.021
Can you drink more?

54:59.105 --> 55:01.857
- Yes.
- I get drunk really easily.

55:02.650 --> 55:04.902
- But...
- All right, everyone. Your glasses.

55:04.985 --> 55:06.696
Let's make a toast! Cheers!

55:06.779 --> 55:08.906
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

55:08.989 --> 55:11.534
- Drink up.
- You can take your alcohol.

55:11.617 --> 55:13.411
- Why don't you have another drink?
- Shall we?

55:14.912 --> 55:16.706
Okay. We're partying
until we drop and die tonight.

55:16.789 --> 55:17.915
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

55:19.208 --> 55:20.876
- Chug your drink!
- Yes!

55:22.837 --> 55:25.256
- Okay.
- Who needs a drink?

55:26.132 --> 55:27.967
Now, another toast!

55:29.009 --> 55:30.469
- Cheers.
- It's the last one.

55:30.553 --> 55:32.096
- The last one.
- The last one!

55:32.179 --> 55:35.349
- It's the last drink here!
- Hey!

55:35.433 --> 55:36.892
That was so good.

55:37.435 --> 55:38.978
Where are we going for round two?

55:39.061 --> 55:41.188
- A karaoke room.
- Let's go karaokeing.

55:42.565 --> 55:44.108
- Mr. Noh. Where's Mr. Noh?
- Yes!

55:47.361 --> 55:48.446
- Hey!
- Come back.

55:48.821 --> 55:50.781
- You can't run away.
- Get back here.

55:50.865 --> 55:52.199
You can't leave today.

55:52.283 --> 55:55.411
- Not today.
- You're the hero tonight.

55:55.494 --> 55:58.748
Drunk as a fish

55:58.831 --> 56:02.334
I am dead drunk

56:02.793 --> 56:06.088
I have fallen

56:06.172 --> 56:09.216
For the scent of your love

56:09.383 --> 56:10.760
I have fallen!

56:11.093 --> 56:14.346
Oh, oh, oh

56:14.430 --> 56:16.348
- All right!
- Sing it!

57:07.691 --> 57:08.692
My goodness.

57:16.450 --> 57:17.952
- Hello?
- Okay!

57:18.994 --> 57:19.995
I'm sorry.

57:20.246 --> 57:23.165
They're holding me back
like today is my last day on earth.

57:23.791 --> 57:25.376
I'm so sorry.

57:26.335 --> 57:28.671
I think it'll take
just a little longer.

57:28.754 --> 57:29.964
Is that so?

57:30.422 --> 57:31.799
Well, I can't help it.

57:32.091 --> 57:34.552
Team dinners are a part of work,
so make sure you stay until the end.

57:38.806 --> 57:40.474
At least he won't be hungry.

57:41.767 --> 57:44.061
That means I'll have to eat

57:44.144 --> 57:46.730
which means my tummy will stick out.

57:46.814 --> 57:48.065
But what can I do?

57:54.405 --> 57:55.406
What?

57:58.075 --> 57:59.285
He said he'd be late.

58:00.452 --> 58:02.204
What is this? A surprise?

58:04.206 --> 58:05.457
You're here already?

58:13.173 --> 58:15.175
- Hey! I'm feeling too great!
- No.

58:15.259 --> 58:16.927
- Just one more bottle.
- Oh, no.

58:17.011 --> 58:19.013
Drunk as a fish

58:19.096 --> 58:20.097
Goodbye!

58:20.180 --> 58:21.515
- Goodbye!
- Boys!

58:21.724 --> 58:23.225
- I'm feeling too great.
- Bye, now.

58:23.309 --> 58:24.894
Time to go!

58:24.977 --> 58:26.896
Come on, man. One more bottle.

58:28.022 --> 58:29.940
- Now.
- All right. I get it.

58:30.024 --> 58:31.150
Okay, then.

58:31.525 --> 58:33.527
Mr. Noh, let's grab
just one more drink.

58:33.611 --> 58:35.696
- Great. I just need one more drink.
- Awesome.

58:35.779 --> 58:37.072
- No.
- What?

58:37.156 --> 58:38.908
That's all for today.
Maybe next time, okay?

58:38.991 --> 58:40.492
- There is no next time.
- There's only today.

58:40.576 --> 58:41.660
- No.
- Where are you going?

58:41.744 --> 58:43.704
- Mr. Noh!
- Just one more drink!

58:43.996 --> 58:45.956
- Mr. Noh!
- Don't go!

58:50.544 --> 58:52.546
You must've been expecting someone.

58:52.630 --> 58:53.923
Yes, I don't know why you're here

58:54.006 --> 58:56.133
but I want you to keep it short
and leave.

58:58.260 --> 58:59.720
I may sound like an idiot

59:00.763 --> 59:03.057
but even as I married
someone who wasn't you

59:03.641 --> 59:05.768
I never once had thought
I had lost you.

59:08.228 --> 59:10.022
That's a selfish thought.

59:10.397 --> 59:12.650
You said you'd be on my side.

59:14.360 --> 59:16.111
I think I lived my life
depending on those words.

59:17.488 --> 59:18.739
You said you were
honoring your words.

59:20.366 --> 59:21.450
I don't care what it is.

59:24.954 --> 59:28.082
I'm getting a divorce.
I told my wife, too.

59:33.963 --> 59:35.422
What do you think you're doing?

59:36.674 --> 59:38.592
What kind of response
did you expect from me?

59:39.301 --> 59:43.305
"Wow, Jae-yeol is divorcing!
I'm going to date him now!"

59:43.514 --> 59:45.265
- Did you think I'd say that?
- I know

59:45.349 --> 59:47.309
I can't get you back
even if I get divorced.

59:48.894 --> 59:50.104
I know

59:50.938 --> 59:52.648
I've lost you for good.

59:54.566 --> 59:57.945
But no matter what I do,
I couldn't let my feelings go.

01:00:00.280 --> 01:00:02.116
The least I can do
is be honest with my feelings.

01:00:03.617 --> 01:00:04.952
That's why I'm divorcing.

01:00:06.286 --> 01:00:07.955
It's not because of you
but because of me.

01:00:09.540 --> 01:00:10.791
It's killing me.

01:00:20.009 --> 01:00:21.385
I regret everything, In-a.

01:00:29.309 --> 01:00:30.936
I'm sorry.
I got here too late, didn't I?

01:00:37.818 --> 01:00:39.278
The one
you had been waiting for is here.

01:00:41.447 --> 01:00:43.949
I'm done talking, so excuse me.

01:01:21.695 --> 01:01:23.781
Wow, you prepared a lot of things.

01:01:25.616 --> 01:01:27.326
Did you make the pasta yourself?

01:01:27.868 --> 01:01:29.661
It looks great.

01:01:31.330 --> 01:01:32.664
I got these delivered.

01:01:37.377 --> 01:01:39.338
Good call. Delivery food is the best.

01:01:39.588 --> 01:01:42.216
Haemu Group's Head of Audit
couldn't have had any time to cook.

01:01:43.300 --> 01:01:45.469
You need to use all your free time
to stare at my face.

01:01:46.678 --> 01:01:47.846
Aren't you going to ask?

01:01:50.015 --> 01:01:51.391
You're in a foul mood.

01:01:51.725 --> 01:01:52.851
And you must be curious.

01:01:53.560 --> 01:01:55.938
Stop beating around the bush
and just ask me.

01:02:03.904 --> 01:02:04.905
I do want to know.

01:02:05.739 --> 01:02:07.324
And yes, I'm in a foul mood.

01:02:08.659 --> 01:02:09.701
But I

01:02:10.369 --> 01:02:12.037
do not want to make myself ask.

01:02:13.330 --> 01:02:14.832
It's probably something
between you two.

01:02:25.134 --> 01:02:26.426
I guess today isn't a good day.

01:02:27.261 --> 01:02:28.720
And you prepared so much.

01:02:35.978 --> 01:02:38.230
Don't drink, and go to sleep early.

01:02:38.939 --> 01:02:40.232
You have to be at work tomorrow.

01:02:41.483 --> 01:02:42.484
Okay?

01:02:43.610 --> 01:02:44.653
I'll get going now.

01:03:47.549 --> 01:03:48.634
Don't go.

01:03:57.434 --> 01:03:58.727
Stay by my side.

01:06:13.153 --> 01:06:14.196
Joo In-a...

01:06:16.031 --> 01:06:18.575
What on earth is she to you?

01:06:20.160 --> 01:06:22.204
She's someone I would die with.

01:06:23.789 --> 01:06:25.916
Can you even give up everything
for that woman?

01:06:26.583 --> 01:06:27.667
If I must.

01:06:28.126 --> 01:06:29.836
Let's say
I back down from Jeon Jae-yeol.

01:06:30.837 --> 01:06:32.339
Can you even have him, A-jeong?

01:06:49.648 --> 01:06:51.858
My gosh. We almost ran late.

01:06:52.109 --> 01:06:53.735
And I'm never late to work.

01:06:53.819 --> 01:06:56.613
And I never wear the same tie
two days in a row.

01:06:57.406 --> 01:06:58.865
That's the thing about dating.

01:06:58.949 --> 01:07:01.451
New definitions are introduced
to your dictionary.

01:07:01.535 --> 01:07:02.911
You're a smooth talker.

01:07:03.620 --> 01:07:04.913
But I can't accept being late.

01:07:05.997 --> 01:07:07.582
Have another great day.

01:07:10.001 --> 01:07:11.711
- You too.
- Thanks.

01:07:19.428 --> 01:07:20.971
Good morning.

01:07:21.054 --> 01:07:22.681
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

01:07:22.764 --> 01:07:23.932
Good morning.

01:07:25.934 --> 01:07:27.227
SENT BY NONAME
REPORTING MS. JOO IN-A

01:07:40.574 --> 01:07:42.701
REPORTING MS. JOO IN-A

01:07:45.871 --> 01:07:47.622
- What?
- What is this?

01:07:47.706 --> 01:07:48.790
Did you see it?

01:07:51.751 --> 01:07:54.171
I'd like to report
on Ms. Joo In-a's private life.

01:07:55.881 --> 01:07:57.841
Ms. Joo In-a remains aloof

01:07:57.924 --> 01:08:00.343
while keeping an eye on others
and punishing them

01:08:00.969 --> 01:08:03.180
but she's actually a hypocrite

01:08:03.722 --> 01:08:05.348
who lives
a very complicated private life.

01:08:06.433 --> 01:08:07.476
I attach

01:08:08.268 --> 01:08:11.438
a picture of Ms. Joo In-a
with her superior, who is married.

01:09:11.289 --> 01:09:14.209
FILING FOR LOVE

01:09:42.320 --> 01:09:43.655
Is the rumor about Ms. Joo true?

01:09:43.738 --> 01:09:47.117
So who's the man in the photo
that you exchanged greetings with?

01:09:47.409 --> 01:09:49.661
I know he's the vice president,
this feels way out of...

01:09:49.744 --> 01:09:52.247
Don't frown. You'll get wrinkles.

01:09:52.330 --> 01:09:54.416
I'll be an iron fortress! Let's go!

01:09:54.499 --> 01:09:55.750
Are you crying?

01:09:55.959 --> 01:09:57.544
You know, Ms. Joo's mail...

01:09:57.627 --> 01:10:00.922
The sender's location was traced
to Mr. Noh Ki-jun's home.

01:10:01.006 --> 01:10:03.800
Are you going to save me
like a knight in shining armor?

01:10:03.883 --> 01:10:04.926
Just say I did it.

01:10:05.010 --> 01:10:07.095
Mr. Noh Ki-jun will face
disciplinary action.

01:10:08.054 --> 01:10:09.306
I'll take responsibility.

01:10:22.777 --> 01:10:24.779
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Jennifer Lim
